From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: T178a checker fixes to 0920/0921: stripes add one invalidation range, cover only scratch growth, depth 0 and 64-bit column test; the backstop does not catch deferred functions; TickWork keeps its fence and lock when a request throws (backstop on)

T178a checker. Always on (0920's stripe path only, which runs only where the session used to end):
- The stripes wrote each GOB with WriteBlockCached: one accumulator entry per GOB, not adjacent
  when the block height is above 0 (~20,000 for a 2304x1152 copy), grown inside the noexcept
  InvalidationAccumulator::Add (std::terminate when that growth fails, in the low-memory state the
  stripes exist for) and replayed one by one at the next FlushCaching. Now WriteBlockUnsafe (the
  same write without the entry) and one AccumulateInvalidation of the range the whole copy added
  (destination address, destination size).
- The catch stripes only when a scratch was smaller than the copy needed; with both (all three
  for block to block) already big enough the std::bad_alloc came from elsewhere (a flush) and is
  rethrown as in T177.
- depth 0: SwizzleSubrectImpl copies nothing; the stripes copied the lines. Now nothing.
- The column test is done in 64 bits (x + count could wrap in 32).
With EDEN_UP_GPU_BADALLOC_BACKSTOP=1 only:
- GpuSplit::ExecuteCaught no longer catches a throw out of a deferred function (Call entry):
  many end in a signal something waits for (SignalFence's synced, MapInOrder's pending map,
  a composite's fences, the list-end flush); dropped half way the waiter waits for ever. Those
  end the session as in T177.
- GPU::TickWork (run inside draws, which the backstop catches): a request that throws still
  advances current_sync_fence and takes sync_request_mutex again before the throw goes on (it
  had been unlocked by hand under a unique_lock, which would unlock it a second time, and every
  later WaitForSyncOperation would wait one request behind).
Off: identical to T177 apart from 0920's catch. maxwell_dma.cpp, gpu_split.cpp and gpu.cpp are not
translation id inputs and no name is added to TranslationSwitches: KEEPS THE STORE.

---
